2025-12-07 11:15:56,832 - src.api.utils.api_logging - INFO - API_CALL_SUCCESS | Endpoint: get_session_messages | User: ANONYMOUS | Status: 200 | Duration: 1.696s | Response: ["id=25 session_id=7 user_id=1 role='user' content='what is transformers' created_at='2025-12-07T05:19:10.677734+00:00'", "id=26 session_id=7 user_id=1 role='assistant' content='The Transformer is a model architecture that uses stacked self-attention and point-wise, fully connected layers for both the encoder and decoder [Figure 1, 3.1]. It is also mentioned in the context of handling problems involving various input and output modalities like text, images, audio, and video [plan to extend the Transformer].' created_at='2025-12-07T05:19:22.443644+00:00'", "id=27 session_id=7 user_id=1 role='user' content='explain in brief' created_at='2025-12-07T05:36:03.878968+00:00'", "id=28 session_id=7 user_id=1 role='assistant' content='The Transformer is a model architecture that uses stacked self-attention. Self-attention layers are used for mapping one variable-length sequence of symbol representations to another sequence of equal length, such as in a typical sequence transduction encoder or decoder [4 Why Self-Attention]. An attention function, a core component, maps a query and a set of key-value pairs to an output, which is computed as a weighted sum of the values [3.2 Attention].' created_at='2025-12-07T05:36:15.578425+00:00'", "id=29 session_id=7 user_id=1 role='user' content='explain layers in transformers' created_at='2025-12-07T05:38:02.983519+00:00'", "id=30 session_id=7 user_id=1 role='assistant' content='The Transformer architecture uses stacked self-attention and point-wise, fully connected layers for both its encoder and decoder [Figure 1, 3.1].\\n\\nBoth the encoder and decoder are composed of a stack of N = 6 identical layers [3.1 Encoder and Decoder Stacks].\\n\\nEach layer in the encoder has two sub-layers:\\n1. A multi-head self-attention mechanism.\\n2. A simple, position-wise fully connected feed-forward network [3.1 Encoder and Decoder Stacks].\\n\\nThe decoder also has a stack of N = 6 identical layers, which include these two sub-layers [3.1 Encoder and Decoder Stacks].\\n\\nResidual connections are employed around each of these two sub-layers, followed by layer normalization. The output of each sub-layer is LayerNorm(x+ Sublayer(x)) [We employ a residual connection]. All sub-layers and embedding layers produce outputs of dimension dmodel = 512 to facilitate these residual connections [To facilitate these residual connections].' created_at='2025-12-07T05:38:12.798366+00:00'"]
