2025-12-07 11:16:53,353 - src.api.utils.api_logging - INFO - API_CALL_SUCCESS | Endpoint: query_documents | User: ANONYMOUS | Status: 200 | Duration: 24.259s | Response: "session_id=7 response={'answer': 'Self-attention, also known as intra-attention, is an attention mechanism that relates different positions of a single sequence to compute a representation of that sequence [Self-attention, sometimes called intra-attention]. It is the approach used in the model described [the approach we take in our model].\\n\\nIn a self-attention layer, all of the keys, values, and queries originate from the same place, specifically the output of the previous layer [The encoder contains self-attention layers]. An attention function, which is a core component, maps a query and a set of key-value pairs to an output. This output is calculated as a weighted sum of the values, where the weight for each value is determined by a compatibility function of the query and the corresponding key [3.2 Attention]. Self-attention layers are compared to recurrent and convolutional layers for mapping variable-length sequences of symbol representations [4 Why Self-Attention].', 'citations': [{'id': 'test_1.pdf', 'score': 0.8273456793196159, 'meta': {'book': 'Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems 30', 'date': '2017', 'page': 1, 'type': 'Conference Proceedings', 'title': 'Attention is All you Need', 'author': 'Ashish Vaswani, Noam Shazeer, Niki Parmar, Jakob Uszkoreit, Llion Jones, Aidan N. Gomez, \u0141ukasz Kaiser, Illia Polosukhin', 'source': 'test_1.pdf', 'created': '2017', 'creator': 'PyPDF', 'editors': 'I. Guyon and U.V. Luxburg and S. Bengio and H. Wallach and R. Fergus and S. Vishwanathan and R. Garnett', 'moddate': '2018-02-12T21:22:10-08:00', 'subject': 'Neural Information Processing Systems http://nips.cc/', 'language': 'en-US', 'lastpage': '6008', 'producer': 'PyPDF2', 'eventtype': 'Poster', 'file_name': 'test_1.pdf', 'file_path': 'data\\\\test_1.pdf', 'firstpage': '5998', 'published': '2017', 'publisher': 'Curran Associates, Inc.', 'page_label': '2', 'description': 'Paper accepted and presented at the Neural Information Processing Systems Conference (http://nips.cc/)', 'total_pages': 11, 'creationdate': '', 'file_path_absolute': 'D:\\\\work\\\\RAG\\\\data\\\\test_1.pdf', 'description-abstract': 'The dominant sequence transduction models are based on complex recurrent orconvolutional neural networks in an encoder and decoder configuration. The best performing such models also connect the encoder and decoder through an attentionm echanisms.  We propose a novel, simple network architecture based solely onan attention mechanism, dispensing with recurrence and convolutions entirely.Experiments on two machine translation tasks show these models to be superiorin quality while being more parallelizable and requiring significantly less timeto train. Our single model with 165 million parameters, achieves 27.5 BLEU onEnglish-to-German translation, improving over the existing best ensemble result by over 1 BLEU. On English-to-French translation, we outperform the previoussingle state-of-the-art with model by 0.7 BLEU, achieving a BLEU score of 41.1.'}, 'pdf_file': 'test_1.pdf', 'pdf_path': 'data\\\\test_1.pdf', 'pdf_link': '/api/files/test_1.pdf'}, {'id': 'test_1.pdf', 'score': 0.8379923440861189, 'meta': {'book': 'Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems 30', 'date': '2017', 'page': 6, 'type': 'Conference Proceedings', 'title': 'Attention is All you Need', 'author': 'Ashish Vaswani, Noam Shazeer, Niki Parmar, Jakob Uszkoreit, Llion Jones, Aidan N. Gomez, \u0141ukasz Kaiser, Illia Polosukhin', 'source': 'test_1.pdf', 'created': '2017', 'creator': 'PyPDF', 'editors': 'I. Guyon and U.V. Luxburg and S. Bengio and H. Wallach and R. Fergus and S. Vishwanathan and R. Garnett', 'moddate': '2018-02-12T21:22:10-08:00', 'subject': 'Neural Information Processing Systems http://nips.cc/', 'language': 'en-US', 'lastpage': '6008', 'producer': 'PyPDF2', '